        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(auth): prioritize explicit models.json apiKey over store profiles",
        "body": "> [!NOTE]\n> **AI-Assisted Contribution:** This PR was prepared and validated with the assistance of an AI coding assistant (Antigravity/Gemini).\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where model auth subsystem ignores explicit `apikey` (literal/secretref) override in `models.json` if store profiles exist (pr #100839).\n\n**Symptom/Behavior:**\nUnless `auth: \"api-key\"` is explicitly set (making `shouldPreferExplicitConfigApiKeyAuth` true), the literal key or SecretRef is ignored during the binding phase (falling through `providerEntryBinding` checks). The function then scans the profile store; if any profile is found for the provider, it overrides the user's explicit `apiKey` configuration.\n\nAffected location: `[src/agents/model-auth.ts](file://src/agents/model-auth.ts#L1024-L1250) (compiled as `dist/model-auth-Bjx4UCgB.js` / `model-auth-DgJcKdh4.js`)`\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nImplemented a surgical fix to resolve the logic discrepancy.\n\n**Solution Overview:**\nHandle `providerEntryBinding.kind === \"literal\"` immediately by returning the literal API key. For SecretRefs, they should be checked and resolved before store profiles are scanned:\n  ```javascript\n  if (providerEntryBinding.kind === \"profile-resolved\") {\n      assertAuthModeAllowedForModel({\n          provider,\n          modelApi: params.modelApi,\n          profileId: providerEntryBinding.auth.profileId ?? provider,\n          mode: providerEntryBinding.auth.mode\n      });\n      return providerEntryBinding.auth;\n  }\n  if (providerEntryBinding.kind === \"literal\") {\n      return {\n          apiKey: providerEntryBinding.apiKey,\n          source: providerEntryBinding.source,\n          mode: \"api-key\"\n      };\n  }\n  ```\n\n## User Impact\n\nCorrects behavior to ensure that: If a user explicitly configures `apiKey` in `models.json` under `models.providers.<provider>.apiKey` as a literal API key string or a SecretRef, this configured credential should take precedence over any general auth profiles in the store for that provider.\n\n## Evidence\n\n<!-- Unit tests and validation logs -->\n\n### Unit Tests / Verification Suite\n- Unit tests in `src/agents/model-auth.profiles.test.ts` and `src/agents/model-auth-label.test.ts` run and pass successfully.\n\n### Real Behavior Proof\n\n#### Standalone Precedence and Label Resolution Verification:\nWe ran a verification script creating a provider entry with a literal `apiKey` in `models.json` alongside a profile in the credentials store. The output proves that both the user-facing status label and the runtime credential resolver align and prioritize the literal key correctly:\n\n```text\n[VERIFICATION] Setup config & store profile:\n  Explicit Config apiKey: \"explicit-literal-key-12345\"\n  General Store profile key: \"profile-key-to-ignore\"\n\n[VERIFICATION] Resolution Results:\n  Status Label:      api-key (models.json)\n  Runtime Key:       explicit-literal-key-12345\n  Runtime Source:    models.json\n\n[SUCCESS] Precedence aligned! Status label reports models.json, and runtime resolves the literal key!\n```\n\n#### Before (Failing Precedence):\n```text\nAssertionError: expected 'profile-key-to-ignore' to be 'explicit-literal-key' // Object.is equality\n\nExpected: \"explicit-literal-key\"\nReceived: \"profile-key-to-ignore\"\n\n ❯ src/agents/model-auth.profiles.test.ts:809:29\n    807|       },\n    808|     });\n    809|     expect(resolved.apiKey).toBe(\"explicit-literal-key\");\n       |                             ^\n    810|     expect(resolved.source).toBe(\"models.json\");\n    811|     expect(resolved.profileId).toBeUndefined();\n```\n\n#### After (Passing Verification):\n```text\nScope: all 159 workspace projects\nLockfile is up to date, resolution step is skipped\nProgress: resolved 0, reused 1, downloaded 0, added 0\nPackages: +1 -173\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProgress: resolved 0, reused 174, downloaded 0, added 1, done\n\n. preinstall$ node scripts/preinstall-package-manager-warning.mjs\n. preinstall: Done\n. postinstall$ node scripts/postinstall-bundled-plugins.mjs\n. postinstall: Done\n. prepare$ node scripts/prepare-git-hooks.mjs\n. prepare: Done\nDone in 2.3s using pnpm v11.2.2\n\n RUN  v4.1.9 /home/dietpi/Developer/openclaw\n\n ✓ |agents| src/agents/model-auth-label.test.ts (12 tests) 165ms\n ✓ |agents| src/agents/model-auth.profiles.test.ts (72 tests) 216ms\n\n Test Files  2 passed (2)\n      Tests  84 passed (84)\n   Start at  12:26:27\n   Duration  1.75s (transform 988ms, setup 305ms, import 2.45s, tests 381ms, environment 0ms)\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/1.1-model-auth-literal-apikey-priority",
